---
title: Plugins
---

A LogIt plugin extends the app with one of six things:

| Family | What it does | Runs as |
|---|---|---|
| `exercise-pack` | Adds exercises to the catalogue | Pure data — not code |
| `progression-algorithm` | Suggests your next sets for an exercise | `suggest(input)` in the sandbox |
| `analytics` | Custom charts/metrics for an exercise | `compute(input)` in the sandbox |
| `nutrition-algorithm` | Turns your goal + data into a calorie target | `computeTargets(input)` in the sandbox |
| `nutrition-analytics` | Weekly recaps, adherence, custom insights | `compute(input)` in the sandbox |
| `widget` | A home-screen card | `compute(input) => WidgetView` in the sandbox |

## How it works

A plugin is **a manifest plus one artifact** — a `bundle.js` for code plugins,
or an `exercises.json` for packs. You publish both to a registry (a static JSON
file), or hand someone the manifest directly.

On install the app fetches the artifact **once**, checks its SHA-256 against the
manifest, and stores it locally. From then on it runs entirely offline. Code is
only ever executed inside a [QuickJS-WASM sandbox](/docs/plugins/trust) — a bare
JavaScript environment with no DOM, no `fetch`, no storage, no timers.

## What you need

- **Node + esbuild** to build a bundle (one file, no imports).
- The types from `@logit/core` for editor help — `@logit/core/domain/progression`,
  `@logit/core/plugins/widgetView`, etc.
- Nothing else. There's no SDK to install and no build server.

Start with the family you want:
[exercise packs](/docs/plugins/exercise-packs) ·
[progression](/docs/plugins/progression) ·
[nutrition](/docs/plugins/nutrition) ·
[widgets](/docs/plugins/widgets)
